     steps=[("Make it safe first.", "If water is visibly leaking, turn off the power at the circuit breaker and close the water supply valve before you inspect anything. Wipe up the water."),
            ("Check the detergent.", "Use automatic dishwasher detergent only, never hand dish soap, and do not overfill the dispenser. Extra suds can leak and trigger the sensor."),
            ("Inspect the door seal.", "Look for food debris on the rubber gasket around the door, or damage that could let water out."),
            ("Check recent changes.", "If the dishwasher was just moved or installed, water may have splashed near the sensor; give it time to dry. If it was just connected to a new garbage disposal, make sure the disposal's knockout plug was removed."),
            ("Check it is level.", "An unlevel dishwasher can let water pool and reach the sensor. Adjust the legs.")],
     after="Once everything is dry, restore power and run a short cycle while you watch for drips.",
